Z||000001||btoth||09-03-2001||12:13 PM||||I used to never get more than 5kbps... the usual was 3k.  Now with my DSL I get anywhere from 10kbps - 100kbps, depending on who I'm downloading files from.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||09-03-2001||12:27 PM||||Well, you connect speed and your transfer rate are two different things.  When I connect at 31.2Kbps (31200 bits per second) I can usually get a transfer rate when downloading of about 3KB/s (3000 bytes per second).  Note the difference in rating.  Since 1 byte = 8 bits, a 3KB/s transfer rate is equal to a 24Kbps transfer rate.  And since you'll never use 100% of your own bandwidth on a download due to communication overhead, etc., that can illustrate the difference.<P>Remember, Windows, like potato chips, is packaged by weight, not volume.  Your mileage may vary.  Some settling occurs during shipping.||||reg||1
